  "contract": [
    "Execute exactly one optical channel: update two live rolling-feature pairs, then use descriptor+88 unsigned modulo to decide whether to publish ratios. Preserve numerator count-1 loads, delayed denominator max(count-13,0) and signed float-bit epsilon clamping.",
    "After the first ratio push, reload second-pair pointers/data. Perform native compare-to-zero FPSCR updates and conditional absolute-bit selection; divide second/first only above the native magnitude threshold. Clear values outside the encoded inclusive ratio interval. Ordinary noinline conditional_divide prevents compiler speculation that otherwise changes DZC/IOC.",
    "Reload the live input pulse after all ratio writes. Multiply by0.5 and convert using defined encoded unsigned saturation/truncation, including NaNs, infinities, negative fractions, subnormals and FP flags. Store only the low16 bits in the decimated signed16 window, preserving cursor/phase/count wrap and actual C memmove.",
    "The root reads the output optical-state pointer before raw sequence/input-state pointers, runs actual optical processing, then invokes explicit motion0x61c48. Reload sequence for the motion call and again after it. Return0 only for sequence%25==24 and wrapped(sequence+1)>=125; otherwise4. No new writable owner or inline assembly."
  ],
